---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout
  title="CTW Studio – Applied Research Software"
  description="CTW Studio designs research software systems that pair academic rigor with cultural-grade design."
  ogDescription="Software for research and society."
  canonical="/"
  current="home"
  homepageStyles
>
    <main id="main-content">
      <section class="ctw-hero ctw-instrument" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="ctw-container ctw-stack">
          <div class="ctw-coordinate"><span>52.3676° N / 4.9041° E</span><span>Amsterdam · working globally</span></div>
          <div class="ctw-hero__grid">
            <div class="ctw-stack">
              <p class="ctw-section-number">01 / Applied practice</p>
              <h1 class="ctw-hero__title" id="hero-title" transition:name="portfolio-lead">Applied research <span class="ctw-display--outline">software.</span></h1>
              <p class="ctw-lede">Software for research and society. Data infrastructure, ML systems, and tools that create <strong>lasting impact</strong>.</p>
              <div class="ctw-cluster">
                <a class="ctw-button" href="#contact">Get in touch →</a>
                <span class="ctw-meta">Available for collaborations</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="studio-stats" aria-label="Studio facts">
              <div class="ctw-stat"><strong class="ctw-stat__value">17</strong><p class="ctw-stat__label">years</p></div>
              <div class="ctw-stat"><strong class="ctw-stat__value">50+</strong><p class="ctw-stat__label">projects</p></div>
              <div class="ctw-stat"><strong class="ctw-stat__value">15</strong><p class="ctw-stat__label">institutions</p></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ctw-cluster">
            <a class="ctw-link ctw-link--standalone" href="/portfolio/">All projects →</a>
            <a class="ctw-link ctw-link--standalone" href="#about">About →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ctw-section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
        <div class="ctw-container ctw-chapter">
          <div class="ctw-chapter__label ctw-stack">
            <p class="ctw-section-number">02 / About</p>
            <p class="ctw-coordinate"><span>Founder</span><span>CTW</span></p>
          </div>
          <div class="studio-about">
            <article class="ctw-stack studio-founder">
              <p class="ctw-label">Jesse Gonzalez</p>
              <h2 class="ctw-heading-lg" id="about-title">Creating a <span class="studio-accent">Technological World.</span></h2>
              <p class="ctw-lede">Founder · Senior Research Software Engineer</p>
              <p>17+ years in software engineering. Currently at Netherlands eScience Center. Master's in Artificial Intelligence and Computer Science.</p>
              <p>Based in Amsterdam, working globally with research institutions and cultural organizations.</p>
              <a class="ctw-link ctw-link--standalone" href="https://jessegonzalez.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Full bio &amp; portfolio ↗</a>
            </article>
            <div class="ctw-stack studio-mission">
              <p class="ctw-label">About CTW Studio</p>
              <p class="ctw-lede">Software for research and society. Tools that help scientists do better research and communities have more voice.</p>
              <p>Open science, sustainable software, technology that serves human flourishing.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ctw-section" id="collaborations" aria-labelledby="collaborations-title">
        <div class="ctw-container ctw-chapter">
          <div class="ctw-chapter__label ctw-stack">
            <p class="ctw-section-number">03 / Collaborations</p>
            <h2 class="ctw-heading-lg" id="collaborations-title">Research software <span class="ctw-display--outline">engineering.</span></h2>
            <p>Partnering with funded research projects to build sustainable, open-source software that advances scientific discovery.</p>
            <a class="ctw-button" href="#contact">Start a collaboration</a>
          </div>
          <ol class="ctw-observations">
            <li class="ctw-observation"><span class="ctw-observation__number">01</span><div><h3 class="ctw-heading-md">Research Data Infrastructure</h3><p>FAIR-compliant data pipelines and architectures for reproducible research at scale.</p></div></li>
            <li class="ctw-observation"><span class="ctw-observation__number">02</span><div><h3 class="ctw-heading-md">ML Systems &amp; Responsible AI</h3><p>Validated, explainable ML systems with proper governance for research and clinical contexts.</p></div></li>
            <li class="ctw-observation"><span class="ctw-observation__number">03</span><div><h3 class="ctw-heading-md">Scientific Visualization &amp; Digital Exhibits</h3><p>Interactive visualizations, 3D environments, and museum-ready digital experiences.</p></div></li>
            <li class="ctw-observation"><span class="ctw-observation__number">04</span><div><h3 class="ctw-heading-md">Collaborative Research Platforms</h3><p>Open-source tools and platforms that support distributed research teams and long-term scholarship.</p></div></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ctw-section" id="how-we-work" aria-labelledby="process-title">
        <div class="ctw-container ctw-stack">
          <p class="ctw-section-number">04 / Our process</p>
          <h2 class="ctw-display--fluid" id="process-title">Working closely with <span class="ctw-display--inverted">research teams.</span></h2>
          <dl class="studio-process">
            <div class="ctw-argument"><dt>01 / Planning</dt><dd><strong>Research goals drive technical strategy.</strong><p>We start with your grant narrative and scientific objectives. Collaborative roadmapping ensures every technical decision serves the research.</p></dd></div>
            <div class="ctw-argument"><dt>02 / Visibility</dt><dd><strong>Transparency at every stage.</strong><p>Regular demos, shared documentation, and open communication. You always know where the project stands and what's next.</p></dd></div>
            <div class="ctw-argument"><dt>03 / Implementation</dt><dd><strong>Design thinking, iterative delivery.</strong><p>Prototypes before polish. We build, test, and refine with your team—solutions shaped by real researcher feedback.</p></dd></div>
            <div class="ctw-argument"><dt>04 / Sustainability</dt><dd><strong>Built to outlast the grant.</strong><p>Open source by default, documentation-first, knowledge transfer. Software that serves the community long after the project ends.</p></dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ctw-section" aria-labelledby="products-title">
        <div class="ctw-container ctw-stack">
          <p class="ctw-section-number">05 / Products</p>
          <h2 class="ctw-display--fluid" id="products-title">Tools we're building <span class="studio-accent">for society.</span></h2>
        </div>
        <p class="ctw-scroll-hint ctw-container" id="product-index-hint">Swipe products to explore →</p>
        <ul class="ctw-project-index studio-products" aria-label="Product index" aria-describedby="product-index-hint">
          <li><a href="https://notidian.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="ctw-label">01 / Knowledge</span><strong class="ctw-heading-md">Notidian</strong><span>Open product ↗</span></a></li>
          <li><a href="https://ideasdiamond.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="ctw-label">02 / Ideas</span><strong class="ctw-heading-md">IdeasDiamond</strong><span>Open product ↗</span></a></li>
          <li><a href="https://nexthuman.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="ctw-label">03 / Capability</span><strong class="ctw-heading-md">NextHuman</strong><span>Coming soon ↗</span></a></li>
          <li><a href="/portfolio/"><span class="ctw-label">Index / Research</span><strong class="ctw-heading-md">Selected projects</strong><span>View all →</span></a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="ctw-section" id="methodology" aria-labelledby="notes-title">
        <div class="ctw-container ctw-stack">
          <p class="ctw-section-number">06 / What collaborators say</p>
          <h2 class="ctw-display--fluid" id="notes-title">Field notes.</h2>
          <div class="studio-quotes">
            <blockquote class="ctw-quote"><p>“Jesse has really been instrumental and decisive in getting our dashboard off the ground. Right from the start, he grasped the overarching concept and got straight down to business.”</p><footer><cite>Josh Colston, PhD</cite><br>Co-Lead, Mine-DD · University of Virginia</footer></blockquote>
            <blockquote class="ctw-quote"><p>“The research tool Collens has proven to be a significant contribution to our research field. We are thoroughly impressed with Jesse's work and work ethic.”</p><footer><cite>Elli Bleeker, PhD</cite><br>Lead Applicant, COLLaiTE · Huygens Institute (KNAW)</footer></blockquote>
            <blockquote class="ctw-quote"><p>“This is what we want as the eScience Center. Work that can have large and long-lasting impact, beyond the project and beyond the discipline.”</p><footer><cite>Valentina Azzara, PhD</cite><br>Section Head · Netherlands eScience Center</footer></blockquote>
            <blockquote class="ctw-quote"><p>“His leadership, initiative, and technical excellence make him a valuable asset to any team he joins.”</p><footer><cite>Kody Moodley, PhD</cite><br>Senior Researcher · Maastricht University</footer></blockquote>
            <blockquote class="ctw-quote"><p>“This is chef's kiss.”</p><footer><cite>Veronica Pang</cite><br>Communication Advisor · Netherlands eScience Center</footer></blockquote>
          </div>
          <div class="ctw-stack studio-partners">
            <p class="ctw-label">Selected partners</p>
            <p>Netherlands eScience Center · KNAW · KNMI · University of Virginia · Maastricht University · Smithsonian Institution</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ctw-closing" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
        <div class="ctw-container ctw-stack">
          <p class="ctw-section-number">07 / Collaborate</p>
          <h2 class="ctw-display--fluid" id="contact-title">We partner with research institutions, cultural heritage organizations, and public-interest initiatives.</h2>
          <p class="ctw-lede">Introduce us to your grant narrative, draft syllabus, or curatorial brief. We reply with a study plan and references.</p>
          <div class="ctw-cluster">
            <a class="ctw-button" href="mailto:contact@ctw.studio">contact@ctw.studio</a>
            <a class="ctw-button ctw-button--secondary" href="https://linkedin.com/in/ctwhome" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a>
          </div>
          <p class="ctw-meta">Amsterdam · working globally · accepting projects 2026-2027</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
</SiteLayout>
